{
  "group": "reject",
  "upstream": "jsonwebtoken@9.0.3",
  "note": "The forgery corpus, and the reason this harness exists. Algorithm confusion (an HS256 token HMAC-signed with the bytes of a public key), alg:none, an empty allowlist, an empty secret, tampered payloads and headers, expiry and nbf, claim mismatches and malformed tokens must ALL fail on both sides. A case where the port succeeds and upstream fails is a vulnerability, not a style difference.",
